The segfault at librdmacm occurs when RDMA_CM_EVENT_ESTABLISHED event with evt->id_priv = NULL is processed by rdma_get_cm_event()

Considering Sean's input, it seems that ctx->file->mut is not used when setting asynchronous rdma events uid, causing in the case of RDMA_CM_EVENT_ESTABLISHED events generated by successful nes_accept to have uid set to zero. Adding mutex protection to code using ctx->uid could fix the issue without reverting changes.   

Thank you,
Tatyana  

